They apply after a reboot. Wrong values can cut this node off for good.␀␀␀␀Enter a password␀␀␀␀The passwords do not match␀␀No spaces␀␀␀Change the admin password? If you lose it you can no longer manage this node over the mesh.␀Reboot the node? It is off the air for about 10 s and forgets guest logins.␀Reboot␀␀start ota␀␀␀Start a firmware update on the node? It opens its own Wi-Fi access point until it is updated or rebooted, and stops repeating meanwhile.␀␀␀␀clear stats␀Reset the node's packet counters?␀␀␀Reset␀␀␀Delete chat with "%s"?
Message history will be cleared.␀Remove channel "%s"?
Leaves it on this device only.␀Delete this chat's entire history?
The chat itself stays.␀␀␀Switch to the external antenna?

Make sure an antenna is actually connected to the external antenna socket first. Transmitting with nothing attached can damage the radio.

Resets to the on-board antenna on every reboot.␀Turn on legacy per-transmit switching?

Diagnostic mode, for comparison only. It transmits on the on-board antenna and listens on the external one, so your outbound signal will be much weaker than your inbound.

Resets to the on-board antenna on every reboot.␀Switch␀␀Always use the external antenna?

The radio will start on the external (MMCX) socket at every boot. Transmitting without an antenna attached can damage the radio.

Only turn this on if your external antenna stays connected.␀Turn on␀250 kHz: %lu %s␀No MediaMesh answered on 250 kHz at␀Repeaters nearby answered on the main mesh, but none on radio2.␀No repeaters answered at all (out of range, or asked too often: try in 2 minutes).␀␀%s %.3f MHz. %s␀MediaMesh found:␀␀␀␀Use this preset?␀␀␀␀%s %s (%lu %s). %s␀␀Use it␀␀of␀␀repeaters nearby run radio2 on␀␀%u %s %u %s %s.␀Repeaters nearby answered, but none has radio2 on.␀␀No radio2 on nearby␀
